Collinear DeltaSpin force and stress regression
=============================================

Test PW DeltaSpin with collinear spin (nspin=2), a Z magnetization
constraint and iterative optimization to target. Force and stress are
computed after both the charge density and constrained atomic magnetic
moments converge to 1e-8. The default solver remains Davidson-subspace.

The previous charge threshold of 1e-6 and magnetic-moment threshold of
1e-4 left force and stress differences larger than the existing reference
tolerances. The revised inputs tighten both convergence targets, set the
initial diagonalization threshold to 1e-10, disable empty-band threshold
smoothing and increase the iteration budgets. The adaptive diagonalization
threshold remains enabled; pw_diag_thr_max is not set. Structure, K points,
pseudopotential, orbitals, cutoff, smearing, mixing and kpar=2 are unchanged.

Reference provenance (2026-10-26)
-------------------------------
The reference uses Davidson-subspace output from a GNU 12.3 / OpenMPI
5.0.10 Release build with four MPI ranks and one OpenMP/BLAS thread.
The build is based on 77f7b4af69934064aa5f4b84267343e9135bc348 plus the
accompanying local PPCG/Davidson and threshold-control fixes. Binary SHA-256:
d9d2914b9f8f793d0da52f28b09a6996ae39483958658dfb72490f51c2b842f1.

Independent PPCG and CG runs used identical inputs except ks_solver.
PPCG and Davidson-subspace converged in 24 SCF steps, CG in 25. Their
final charge errors were 9.22e-9, 8.47e-9 and 5.09e-9; complete-space
magnetic moment RMS errors were 7.28e-9, 4.97e-9 and 2.66e-9 Bohr magnetons.
The final printed atomic moments independently satisfy the same target.

Maximum differences across all three solver pairs:
  total energy:             1.20e-8 eV
  force absolute-value sum:  6.0e-6 eV/Angstrom
  stress absolute-value sum: 7.80e-5 kbar
  individual force entry:   1.38e-6 eV/Angstrom
  individual stress entry:  4.27e-5 kbar

The original reference-check tolerances remain 1e-7 eV, 1e-4 eV/Angstrom
and 1e-3 kbar. The reference contains the same four properties as before;
timing output is not used as a numerical reference. All three tightened
calculations differ from the old stress reference by about 8.764 kbar in
the absolute-value sum, establishing the need for the reference update.
